this is the second  longest running race on the continent  now most cars are going to run  on gasoline this car the bentley  continental gt3 is going to run it on  biofuel  [Music]  so why is pikes peak so iconic i mean  it's a little obscure  but it's a big deal i think it's the  adventure and the challenge  you you can go to a traditional race  course and your targets are almost going  to be the same all the time  you've got loads and loads of  information  you you come here and you're not just  challenging the course you're  challenging the weather patterns and  everything  it's a risk factor if you're going to  get rewarded by  what the weather is going to give you um  but if you get it right and you've done  your homework as we have done and  proved to be so fast in practice  if everything goes right on race day the  reward is  unparalleled to any event in the world  tell me what this runs on this is a very  special type of fuel it's not gasoline  yeah this is a biofuel that we're  running here and it's part of you know  the green  touch element that the program has been  born from  um you know with the future of the  automotive industry going to  electric this is an alternative for any  standard combustion engine car  that currently exists you would have  seen last year that we announced our  beyond 100 strategies so  as a brand we really brought into a  renewable future  we also recognize that it's going to  take quite a few years you know  for the world to develop and for you  know battery electric cars to become you  know really  commonplace and usable etc so we see  um renewable fuels as an alternative  that could be used you know in parallel  with electrification um as a way to  allow both  you know the customers are buying our  cars today cars like the w12 or the v8s  to continue to use these cars  as well as customers who've had their  cars for many years and what a renewable  fuel does is it  it allows you to to basically you're  recapturing co2 from the atmosphere  whether you go via you know bioethanol  or whether you go by a property or to  capture like a real e fuel  it allows you to to generate a fuel that  that is not bad for the environment  and so we started to look at that and  we're really using this as a bit of a  test bed and a launch of that strategy  for bentley so  tell me specifically about this car  what we've done is we've taken a  standard gt3 race car  and then we've we've upped that a little  bit in the regs here you're a little bit  more downforce so we've got about a  30 increase in in overall downfalls from  this car  you know really mixed up against what  the regulations allow you to do  and then we've done a lot of work on the  engine particularly to allow it to run  well in this type of environment so the  real challenge here  is to be able to get your power both at  the start and then right at the top as  well and so we're talking what elevation  change  yeah it's a good six thousand feet of  elevation change  and yeah that's a particular challenge  for a you know for an engine so we've  done some work on the  on the engine we've added some more you  know some more injectors and a bit of  water injection as well  and that enables us to keep it cool and  keep it running all the way to the top  does the biofuel make any difference in  the way that the car  handles accelerates drives  there was some small mapping things  because this is a race engine  that the engine calibrator had needed to  do but outside of that the performance  of the engine there's zero loss it's  absolutely amazing  it depends on the specification of the  fuel so like with a standard fuel you  can specify fuel and you can blend them  up to get the performance that you want  so of course pike's peak is very special  your high altitude you're running a  turbocharged car here  so we're looking for a fuel that we can  blend up to be a race fuel  but still with a very high percentage of  renewable content in that and that's  really the challenge for  the challenge for this and then yeah as  time progresses we think  we'll see that we'll be able to get  fuels that are blended to match what you  want  in your road car as well i love that so  the idea is  potentially this fuel could be run in  any bentley on the road  the ideal for us eventually is to have a  fuel that is a plug and play  to your standard fuel specifications and  obviously for a for a racetop car you've  got different types of fuels  so at the moment we've been testing both  in the in the road car side and then the  in the racecar side you get different  blends of fuel and you know different  sources and  um you're depending where it comes from  you can get certain percentages of  renewability  and you know as that technology evolves  you know we think it's a great  opportunity for people to be able to run  their combustion engine cars  and still be good for the planet okay so  what's next for bentley that's an  interesting question  because you know whatever we do from a  motorsport side we really wanted to be  part of our  of our beyond 100 strategy so we're  looking at various options you know for  motorsport in the future  um and also for you know for our road  cars as well so  there's lots of there's lots of  opportunity working really hard on you  know on electrification we've got some  really fascinating cars coming in next  in the next few years so look out for  them and there's a broad spectrum of  what bentley can do and this is really  trying to demonstrate that bit more  aggressive out the edge of what bentley  is it's not just the queen  it's also about racing we can go from  that complete absolute luxury into the  spectrum  right up to you know the sporty unit  we've got a heritage in in motorsports  and we want to show  you know i want to show everybody that  we can cover that whole breadth of what  bentley is and continue to that in the  future and as we electrify and as we  go forward you know we continue to want  to have that breadth of of our brand  so from pikes peak this is behind the  wheel  for more follow us on your favorite  platforms  you

